# PR review bot replies

Same standard as Australian Rates: **`WORKFLOW.md`** step 6.

**Summary:** for every substantive thread from automated reviewers, reply with the disposition (Implemented + SHA / Deferred + reason / Declined + reason) **and resolve the thread on GitHub**. This repo enables `required_conversation_resolution`, so a replied-but-unresolved thread stays blocked. The repository feedback gate intentionally requires both an explicit disposition and resolution; resolution alone is insufficient. Green CI alone does not replace thread closure.

**Self-healing — never push empty "re-trigger" commits.** `bot-feedback-gate` is single-shot and intentionally has no shared concurrency group because GitHub can replace an older pending run even with `cancel-in-progress: false`. It reacts to created, edited, and deleted inline review comments and retries the reply-before-resolution race four times at five-second intervals. Stale events for closed PRs exit cleanly. GitHub emits no webhook on *resolve*, so after a resolve-only round re-run via an inline review-thread reply (`pull_request_review_comment`, runs on the PR head), a push, or `gh run rerun <run-id>` of the existing PR-head run. A top-level PR comment (`issue_comment`) and a bare `gh workflow run … -f pr_number` both run against the default branch, so their check won't attach to the PR head.

**Gate:** `npm run pr:bot-feedback-check -- --pr <n>` must exit **0** before squash merge. Use `npm run pr:arm-and-park -- --pr <n>` for authoritative progression and exact-base enforcement. Only **`bot-feedback-gate`** is the universal protected review context; reviewer vendors, Qwen, and **`bot-presence-gate`** are advisory and never merge-blocking. Post-merge: `npm run pr:bot-feedback-audit`, then add in-thread dispositions and a fix PR if late feedback reveals a defect.
